// 02 - Arithmetic and operator precedence
//
// Thunder integers are 64-bit. * / % bind more tightly than + and -, and
// operators of equal precedence group from left to right.
//
// Try it: open the AST tab. Notice how the tree's shape, not the order of the
// characters, decides which operation happens first.

println(1 + 2 * 3)          // 7, not 9
println((1 + 2) * 3)        // parentheses change the shape of the tree
println(7 - 2 - 1)          // (7 - 2) - 1 = 4: left-associative
println(17 / 5, " ", 17 % 5)  // integer division and remainder
println(-7 / 2)             // division rounds toward zero: -3

// A longer expression with nested parentheses:
println(10 + 5 * ((12 / 2) * 5) - -12)
